Aurelia — Curated Gatherings
Smart Event Management Platform — Final Submission (Modules 1–4)

Internee: Mahzaib Irshad Internship ID: ZYNVEX-CERT-1049 Program: Front-end Development Batch: 3 Submission window: Aug 24 – Sep 20, 2026

📌 About the Project

Aurelia is a responsive, web-based event management platform for high-profile, invitation-style events (galas, executive summits, private launches, and bespoke private commissions like weddings and corporate off-sites). It lets users browse upcoming events, view full event details, search and filter by category/date/location, register for events, manage their registrations from a personal dashboard, and submit private event enquiries — all through a single-page, data-driven front end.

✅ Full Feature List (All Modules)

Module 1 — Homepage & Event Listing

Responsive navbar, hero section, and footer
Custom visual identity (dark theme, gold accent, Fraunces + Inter typography)
Event data model (EVENTS array) as a single source of truth
Reusable event card component, rendered dynamically from data
Featured Events section (auto-generated from the same data)
Departures ticker — a live-style board showing the next 4 upcoming events

Module 2 — Event Details, Search & Filtering

Full event details view (image/glyph, category, title, date, location, seats left, description)
Card-to-details navigation with correct event context on every click
Live search bar — filters by title, location, or category as the user types
Category filter chips, auto-generated from event data
Combined search + category filtering (AND logic)
Empty-state message when no events match

Module 3 — Registration System

RSVP registration form (name, email, phone, seats requested)
Client-side validation — required fields, email format, phone format, with inline errors
Duplicate-registration check (per event + email)
Registrations persisted to localStorage with a generated reference code
Confirmation screen showing the reference code and seat count

Module 4 — Dashboard, Polish & Deployment

"My Invitations" dashboard — lists all confirmed registrations, joined with event details
Cancel/withdraw a registration directly from the dashboard
Site-wide UI/UX polish: modal fade-in animation, toast notifications, consistent focus states, prefers-reduced-motion support
Cross-browser and cross-device responsiveness testing and fixes
Final code cleanup, comments, and deployment

Additional Features 

Private Event Enquiry ("Request Access" / "Plan Your Own Event") — a separate form for bespoke bookings (weddings, corporate events, private dinners, etc.), independent of the public event roster, also persisted to localStorage with its own reference code
Private Commissions section — a dedicated homepage banner directing prospective hosts to the enquiry form
Excitement & polish pass — ambient animated hero background, scroll-reveal animations on section entry, animated stat counters (events hosted, cities, guests, return rate), rotating client testimonial quotes, 3D tilt effect on event cards, and a closing call-to-action banner
Mobile navigation menu for small screens
🛠️ Tech Stack
Tool	Purpose
HTML5	Page structure
CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid)	Layout, responsive design, animations
JavaScript (ES6+)	DOM rendering, data handling, form logic, view routing
Web Storage API (localStorage)	Persisting registrations and private-event requests client-side
Google Fonts	Fraunces (display serif), Inter (body sans-serif)
Git & GitHub	Version control and deployment (GitHub Pages)

No frameworks, build tools, or backend — a fully static, vanilla front-end application.

📁 Project Structure
